{%- comment -%}
  NON Somm — the mobile bottom sheet.

  Rendered ONCE per page, from theme.liquid, on the templates that carry an
  entry point. Every mobile Somm trigger on the page opens this one sheet, so
  there is a single conversation rather than one per component: tapping the
  hero, then a triptych tile, then the PDP entry continues the same thread
  instead of starting three.

  It is a [data-non-somm-root] in its own right. somm.js resolves a form's
  answer panel, stream and picks by walking up to the nearest root, so the
  sheet's form writes into the sheet and the hero's writes into the hero,
  without either knowing the other exists.

  DESKTOP IS NOT TOUCHED. The sheet is display:none above the mobile
  breakpoint and no desktop control opens it — the desktop Somm stays the
  inline component it has always been. display:none rather than a visual hide
  is deliberate: it takes the sheet out of the accessibility tree too, so a
  screen reader on a wide viewport never meets two copies of the same Somm.

  It never opens by itself. Opening is always a customer action.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="non-sheet" data-non-sheet hidden>
  {%- comment -%}
    The scrim closes on tap. It is not the only way out — there is a labelled
    close button and Escape — because a scrim tap is invisible to anyone who
    cannot see it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="non-sheet__scrim" data-non-sheet-close tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div
    class="non-sheet__panel"
    role="dialog"
    aria-modal="true"
    aria-labelledby="non-sheet-title"
    data-non-sheet-panel
    data-non-somm-root>
    <div class="non-sheet__grab" data-non-sheet-grab aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <div class="non-sheet__head">
      <span class="non-mono non-eyebrow" id="non-sheet-title">{{ 'sections.somm.heading' | t }}</span>
      {%- if settings.somm_endpoint != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The live dot only when an endpoint is actually configured. A store
          with no Worker set would otherwise claim a service it does not have,
          which the brief rules out and which would be a lie on the page.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <span class="non-sheet__live" data-non-sheet-live>
          <span class="non-sommbox__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'sections.somm.heading' | t }}</span>
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}
      <button type="button" class="non-sheet__x" data-non-sheet-close>
        <span aria-hidden="true">&times;</span>
        <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'sections.somm.close' | t }}</span>
      </button>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      The scrolling half. Only this scrolls: the field and the product action
      stay pinned, so the way to buy never scrolls away mid-conversation.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="non-sheet__scroll" data-non-sheet-scroll>
      <p class="non-sheet__opener" data-non-sheet-opener hidden></p>

      <div class="non-somm__answer" data-non-somm-answer hidden>
        <p class="non-somm__stream" data-non-somm-stream></p>
        <div class="non-somm__picks" data-non-somm-picks hidden></div>
        {% render 'ask-form' %}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="non-sheet__foot">
      {%- comment -%}
        PERSISTENT COMMERCE CONTEXT. On a product page the bottle being
        discussed stays buyable while the sheet is open, so a conversation
        cannot become a detour away from the purchase. Filled in by
        somm-sheet.js from the trigger's context; hidden everywhere else.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="non-sheet__ctx" data-non-sheet-ctx hidden></div>

      <div class="non-sheet__seeds" data-non-sheet-seeds></div>

      <form
        class="non-sheet__ask"
        data-non-somm
        data-somm-context="home"
        role="search">
        <label class="visually-hidden" for="non-sheet-input">
          {{ 'sections.somm.placeholder' | t }}
        </label>
        <input
          id="non-sheet-input"
          class="non-somm__input"
          type="search"
          name="query"
          autocomplete="off"
          enterkeyhint="send"
          data-non-somm-input
          placeholder="{{ 'sections.somm.placeholder' | t | escape }}">
        <button type="submit" class="non-sheet__send">
          <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
          <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'sections.somm.ask' | t }}</span>
        </button>
      </form>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script src="{{ 'somm-sheet.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
